ry of cell differentiation</article-title><source>Bull Math Biol</source><year>1997</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>196</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8980305</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Qu</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Abi Haidar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ensman</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Tuncay</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jolly</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ortoleva</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cancer onset and progression: a genome-wide, nonlinear dynamical systems perspective on onconetworks</article-title><source>J Theor Biol</source><year>2007</year><volume>246</volume><fpage>234</fpage><lpage>244</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17289080</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mendoza</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A network model for the control of the differentiation process in Th cells</article-title><source>BioSystems</source><year>2006</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>101</fpage><lpage>114</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16386358</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kauffman</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metabolic stability and epigenesis in randomly constructed genetic nets</article-title><source>Journal of Theoretical Biology</source><year>1969</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>437</fpage><lpage>467</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5803332</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><pers